{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MIC",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear ye now what the LORD saith; Arise, contend thou before the mountains, and let the hills hear thy voice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear ye, O mountains, the LORD'S controversy, and ye strong foundations of the earth: for the LORD hath a controversy with his people, and he will plead with Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my people, what have I done to thee? and wherein have I wearied thee? testify against me,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I brought thee out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed thee from the house of servants; and I sent before thee Moses, Aaron, and Miriam.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my people, remember now what Balak king of Moab consulted, and what Balaam the son of Beor answered him from Shittim to Gilgal; that ye may know the righteousness of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherewith shall I come before the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bow myself before the high God? shall I come before him with burnt-offerings, with calves of a year old?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with ten thousands of rivers of oil? shall I give my first-born ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my transgression, the fruit of my body ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sin of my soul?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath shown thee, O man, what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good; and what the LORD doth require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD'S voice crieth to the city, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the man of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom shall see thy name: hear ye the rod, and who hath appointed it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are there yet the treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked, and the scant measure ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " abominable?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall I count ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure with the wicked balances, and with the bag of deceitful weights?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the rich men thereof are full of violence, and the inhabitants thereof have spoken lies, and their tongue ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " deceitful in their mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore also will I make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sick in smiting thee, in making ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " desolate because of thy sins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt eat, but not be satisfied; and thy casting down ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the midst of thee; and thou shalt take hold, but shalt not deliver; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which thou deliverest will I give up to the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt sow, but thou shalt not reap; thou shalt tread the olives, but thou shalt not anoint thee with oil; and sweet wine, but shalt not drink wine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the statutes of Omri are kept, and all the works of the house of Ahab, and ye walk in their counsels; that I should make thee a desolation, and the inhabitants thereof an hissing: therefore ye shall bear the reproach of my people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
